    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d543">

                <pb facs="0864" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3268: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Peru</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Moore</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-27T12:00:00-05:00">February 27,
                        1929—noon</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>16. Your 21, February 26, 3 p.m. Telegraph us immediately when President Leguia
                    submits the report to Ambassador Figueroa. <pb facs="0865" n="729"
                        xml:id="pg729"/> I assume that it will be the same as your 19, February 21,
                    4 p.m. How is he going to get the proposition of $3,500,000 before Ambassador
                    Figueroa?</p>
                <p>I am obliged to you for your prompt message.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
